Sub-Task 11: Flink SQL Timestamp Cleaning + Full Pipeline Activation
====================================================================
Date       : 2026-10-07
Status     : PASS

ROOT CAUSE RESOLVED
-------------------
Producer emits _produced_at in ISO-8601 format with microseconds + UTC offset:
  "2026-10-01T13:32:07.539165+00:00"

All Flink SQL jobs used TO_TIMESTAMP(_produced_at, 'yyyy-MM-dd''T''HH:mm:ss')
which failed to parse this format. Because json.ignore-parse-errors=true was
set, all records were silently dropped → 0 read-records in every job.

FIX APPLIED (Flink SQL as the cleaning layer):
  REPLACE(SUBSTRING(`_produced_at`, 1, 19), 'T', ' ')
  → strips microseconds + TZ offset
  → replaces 'T' separator with space
  → yields "2026-10-01 13:32:07" parseable by TO_TIMESTAMP(,'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss')

ADDITIONAL FIXES
----------------
1. DROP TABLE IF EXISTS before every CREATE TABLE — prevents stale catalog reuse
2. SET execution.checkpointing.interval = 30s on ALL jobs (was missing on 02/03/04)
3. SET table.exec.source.idle-timeout = 10s on all event-time jobs
4. job_02 switched from FOR SYSTEM_TIME AS OF to INTERVAL JOIN (correct for 2 Kafka sources)
5. MinIO buckets created via mc alias set (minio-init was using deprecated mc config host add)
6. TaskManager scaled to 8 slots (was 4 — not enough for 6 concurrent jobs)
7. job_03 scan.startup.mode = latest-offset (KPI for live dashboard, not historical replay)
8. Flink SQL philosophy: each job documents WHY each transformation exists

